  {
   "beat_id": "B02",
   "act": "FIELD-OBJECTIVE",
   "narration_text": "Field one: the objective. One sentence naming the outcome, not the process. Not 'summarize the reports' \u2014 that describes the process. 'Produce a two-page board summary covering program milestones, budget status, and open risks for Q3 2024' \u2014 that names the outcome. The objective anchors scope for every field that follows.",
   "shot": {
    "type": "REMOTION",
    "source": "own",
    "motion": "callout-reveal",
    "media": "media/B02.mp4",
    "manim": {
     "scene_class": "Scene_B02_ClaudeLiamSeven",
     "scenes_file": "scenes_std.py",
     "rendered": {
      "out": "media/B02.mp4",
      "at": "2026-07-25T10:43:36.922191"
     }
    }
   },
   "new_visual_element": "Field 1: Objective \u2014 outcome not process",
   "spark_line": "Outcome, not process.",
   "estimated_duration_s": 13,
   "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
   "actual_duration_s": 18.92,
   "build": {
    "status": "SLATE",
    "src": null,
    "filled_by": null,
    "at": "2026-07-16T06:57:36",
    "needs": "PIPELINE \u2192 fill_slates/remotion_scenes for B02"
   }
  },
  {
   "beat_id": "B03",
   "act": "DECISION-RULES",
   "narration_text": "Field five is the one most people skip: decision rules. What does Cowork do when two sources contradict each other? When a number is ambiguous? When a section is missing entirely? Without decision rules, Cowork resolves conflicts silently using its own judgment \u2014 and you find the error in the output, not in a warning.",
   "shot": {
    "type": "REMOTION",
    "source": "own",
    "motion": "callout-reveal",
    "media": "media/B03.mp4",
    "manim": {
     "scene_class": "Scene_B03_ClaudeLiamSeven",
     "scenes_file": "scenes_std.py",
     "rendered": {
      "out": "media/B03.mp4",
      "at": "2026-07-25T10:43:40.657523"
     }
    }
   },
   "new_visual_element": "Field 5: Decision rules \u2014 conflict flagged, not resolved",
   "spark_line": "Flag conflicts. Never resolve.",
   "estimated_duration_s": 13,
   "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
   "actual_duration_s": 16.66,
   "build": {
    "status": "SLATE",
    "src": null,
    "filled_by": null,
    "at": "2026-07-16T06:57:36",
    "needs": "PIPELINE \u2192 fill_slates/remotion_scenes for B03"
   }
  },
  {
   "beat_id": "B04",
   "act": "STOP-CONDITIONS",
   "narration_text": "Field seven: stop conditions. What should Cowork do when a source is missing, a file is inaccessible, or a number does not add up? The answer is always: pause and report, not guess and continue. Stop conditions are the brief's safety valve \u2014 the instruction Cowork follows when things go wrong.",
   "shot": {
    "type": "REMOTION",
    "source": "own",
    "motion": "callout-reveal",
    "media": "media/B04.mp4",
    "manim": {
     "scene_class": "Scene_B04_ClaudeLiamSeven",
     "scenes_file": "scenes_std.py",
     "rendered": {
      "out": "media/B04.mp4",
      "at": "2026-07-25T10:43:44.648131"
     }
    }
   },
   "new_visual_element": "Field 7: Stop conditions \u2014 missing sources \u2192 pause, not guess",
   "spark_line": "Missing source = pause.",
   "estimated_duration_s": 12,
   "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
   "actual_duration_s": 15.66,
   "build": {
    "status": "SLATE",
    "src": null,
    "filled_by": null,
    "at": "2026-07-16T06:57:36",
    "needs": "PIPELINE \u2192 fill_slates/remotion_scenes for B04"
   }
  },
  {
   "beat_id": "B05",
   "act": "VERDICT",
   "narration_text": "The test: could a stranger read this brief and know exactly what Cowork may do, what it may access, and what it must not do? Seven fields. Objective, sources, forbidden data, output format, decision rules, verification criteria, stop conditions. Missing fields guarantee bad output. Present fields guarantee a fixable spec.",
   "shot": {
    "type": "REMOTION",
    "source": "own",
    "motion": "stagger",
    "remotion": {
     "pattern": "CoworkTaskView",
     "props": {
